  "notes": "Quotes, characters and the mentions inside quotes are imported from PDNC at e507a27; every other item is Claude's draft and pending review. The young woman is Agnes Fleming and the nurse Old Sally (Mrs. Thingummy), as PDNC attributes their lines; one key from the start (guidelines section 2). The infant is 'it' / 'the child' / 'the infant' and links to Oliver. The narrator's 'I' has no entity (null). 'a certain town' is a provisional key: Dickens never names it here. Agnes MOTHER_OF Oliver was drafted on the nurse's 'Think what it is to be a mother' and deleted on review (team decision, 2026-10-16): the line makes Agnes a mother in general but never names the child, and the chapter only shows the tie (she asks to see the child, kisses it and dies), which section 7 does not allow as evidence. Predicate descriptions ('a parish child the orphan of a workhouse') are not mentions. 'her' in 'thirteen children of her own' (Q-line of the nurse) keeps PDNC's reading, Agnes, the grammatical subject; the drafter read it as the nurse's own children. Ambiguous; reviewers decide.",
